my name is Margaret Mabry and I am the  member for Walden Field Ward and the  cabinet member for communities I was  elected in May 2015  my days are very flexible and can change  at late noticed sometimes I start at  7:00 in the morning I leave home and I  don't arrive back until late at night  the meetings can be very variable  sometimes I can have meetings all days  sometimes I can have one in the morning  one in the afternoon and one in the  evening it's very very variable and  that's one of the things that I enjoy  about being a councillor it's not 95  it's very variable the meetings can be  in the council chamber for full council  meeting they can be in a small committee  they can be with our partners they can  be within the ward they can be at parish  councils they can be with Suffolk County  Council  they are really variable so why did you  become a counselor because I was asked  to and after I had stopped laughing  because I found it he really funny I  asked the reason why and it was because  I had an opinion I attended parish  council meetings and I would ask  questions and I would have some input  into those meetings only during public  session obviously and basically I was  just asked if I would if I would stand I  had to think about it because I was  concerned about time whether I would  like to be pinned down from 9:00 to 5:00  but I was assured it wasn't like that  and I can guarantee it isn't I got  involved by attending parish council  meetings and I think if you have a real  interest in a subject the that you write  to your local board member  and also make your views clear at the  parish council meeting that is the that  is the first way in otherwise if we go  down a political route then obviously if  you're interested in a political party  what they stand for their values are the  same as yours then I would suggest that  you joined your political party and got  involved there with their meetings and  their fundraising events whatever they  are doing if you are really interested  in democracy then you should stand to be  a counselor it is no point complaining  to account solar water to your parish to  your district to your County if you have  an opinion and you have never lost it  and if you are really serious about  helping others being involved then  standing for council is for you  I have lived within the Baber district  for almost 40 years raised my children  here my children went to school here  they have been they have been successful  and happy here and I have been happy  here the whole district of Baber has a  vast expanse of country  of the coast of people if you want to  disappear for it for a moment and find  your own little corner with nobody it's  still possible it just has such a  variety and if we continue to enjoy the  area then it will continue to thrive the  very special occasion is that it's 90  years since the act of equal  representation which gave men and women  equal opportunity to vote this year is  looks over hundreds anniversary when  that some of the first women received  the vote there were conditions attached  to this voting system and it was that  women  property and be over the age of 30 and  hence it wasn't until 10 years later  that there was the equal representation  fact I also believe that this year is  very important  we are also witnessing the anniversary  of the arm of Armistice in 1918 women  had a very important role during the  First World War they took on the jobs  that men historically had done which  allowed the men to fight on the front  and women stayed at home and continued  to support the country I believe this is  a very important reason to acknowledge  democracy this week we need we need more  women in politics that I believe  currently at Weber we have 12 out of 43  and it would be nice to see a few  younger women stepping up and into the  shoes of those that who have gone before  we install so remember during 1918 that  the suffragettes and suffragists were  also working towards the votes for women  next year we have district council  elections and it would be really good to  see more women coming forward to stand  for these positions there there are  always people who can advise and who can  who can help and if you don't step  forward then there won't be women in  politics in the future I am a cabinet  member I was appointed a year ago and  this does involve much more work that is  much more like a full-time time job and  I think that perhaps the public find  this difficult to understand because  councillors are volunteers we are  classed as volunteers we do do the job  the majority of us because we believe  that that we can help people and that we  can make a difference however once you  step up and you become a cabinet member  it is slightly more structured and you  find you have more emails you have more  paperwork to read you have more  decisions to make and decision-making is  something that you must be comfortable  with there is no point in making a  decision and then worrying for days  afterwards  part of a district counselors job is  local casework and this is where you  help residents who have a particular  issue this can be widely different from  sorting out a tree perhaps that is  impacting on their life it can be trying  to work out who owns a piece of land it  can be helping someone who has a housing  issue that is a very important part of  being a district counselor you must like  people you must want to help people and  you must really enjoy solving those  problems having been elected a counselor  I found it a huge privilege the day that  I knew from their vote that I had been  elected I just could not stop smiling  because it was a really happy time for  me but then you think afterwards what  you've let yourself in for and you  realize it is a huge public privilege it  is a huge honor and at times it is very  humbling but very very enjoyable and if  anyone has an inkling to stand as a  counselor  would encourage them to do so
 

